{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law","id":824164,"title":"Feeding and the Law","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-05T04:15:24-08:00","id":824164,"title":"Feeding and the Law","content":"It may be a silly question... oh... alright this is a silly question. Anyway I realized that in order to suppress his hunger, a beast need to commit actions which thecnically are all crimes which I suppose soon or later, will lead the police at the beast's house door. My question is: there's no way to feed in a more reserved way and without break laws?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T04:51:22-08:00","id":824179,"title":"","content":"Best way to feed without breaking the law is Family Dinner, but there are non-criminal methods.<br /> <br /> Collectors don't require criminal activity, as seen in the descriptions in chapter 3.<br /> Tyrants don't require criminal activity, as seen in the descriptions in chapter 3.<br /> Predators... they nearly always require criminal activity. But you could hurt someone's social life.<br /> Nemesis, hard to do without criminal activity.<br /> Ravager, they can feed without criminal activity by being smart, but generally only at low-satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:28:49-08:00","id":824201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law#post824164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be a silly question... oh... alright this is a silly question. Anyway I realized that in order to suppress his hunger, a beast need to commit actions which thecnically are all crimes which I suppose soon or later, will lead the police at the beast's house door. My question is: there's no way to feed in a more reserved way and without break laws?</div> </div> </div> </div>Collectors: You get perfectly legal collectors in real life. An example of feeding would be going to an auction and snapping up bids at the last second, just when whoever it is thinks that it's in the bag.<br /> <br /> Tyrants: Corporate exec. Enough said.<br /> <br /> Predators: Trickier, but you could hunt criminals as a consultant for the police. You could (as milo v3 said) be a social predator. It just takes a little imagination.<br /> <br /> Nemesis: Similar to Predator. Also, you could be an extremely strict schoolteacher. Remember, they feed off the <i>fear</i> of punishment, not the act itself.<br /> <br /> Ravager: You need not ruin physical things. In politics, you could pull apart an opponent's following and power base. You could ruin relationships, the masks people use to hide themselves (a child abuser's respectable front comes to mind...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T08:20:52-08:00","id":824328,"title":"","content":"Friendly reminder that, in the first draft, at least, a sample Tyrant was a health inspector who fed by being incorruptible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:04:33-08:00","id":824358,"title":"","content":"Well as a nemesis being a cop would be rather beneficial since you don't need to outside the law most of the time. Just go into the division that best supports your hunger and go for it. Heck the rules on feeding imply that a major bust involving a decent amount of people could do wonders for your feeding.<br /> <br /> As has been pointed out a tyrant only needs to establish they're in control, so any situation you get in where another person or group of people are forced to worry about you deciding to act can fit there.<br /> <br /> Predators are trickier, but bounty hunter is a solid one there, as could investigator, or auditor.<br /> <br /> Ravager is the trickiest, but as long as you don't limit yourself to the destruction of physical things you're solid.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna be honest law enforcement is an amazing field for Beasts. I've got one idea for a Collector who basically views the evidence locker as his hoard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:15:06-08:00","id":824365,"title":"","content":"If you don't want to or can't work in law enforcement and the like, be creative with your powers. Hide evidence of your crimes in your Lair, burn it with Dragonfire or eat it with Limb From Limb. Discourage people from calling the police by using Nightmares. Ask your Brood for help. The list goes on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:09:28-08:00","id":824409,"title":"","content":"Nemesis cop taking down criminals come to mind. Predator as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:41:38-08:00","id":824434,"title":"","content":"You do realize that having the Criminal Justice System actually work with any degree of efficiency would dramatically change the tone of the game, right? I mean, it's one thing to have your PCs get arrested or even imprisoned in the course of playing the game, but a lot of the overall themes of CoD rely on the system being corrupt, inefficient, and ultimately incapable of getting positive results. Nevermind that escape is just a few die rolls away for most Beasts, and that staying on the run is easier than you'd think, what you have to ask yourself, 'is what I'm about to do worth it for the cops to pursue?&quot; Most of the time, short of noticeable property damage or readily discovered victims with clearly mundane injuries and/or relatively sober and lucid accounts of what happened, there is very little the authorities can do to turn a reported crime into an arrest, much less a conviction.<br /> <br /> Long story short: if you have any degree of crossover, or play smart, the strict legality of what you are doing to Feed should not be an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T15:59:04-08:00","id":824642,"title":"","content":"Ravager would also work as a demolition expert, taking down buildings people want to keep around, or a logger cutting down trees that certain people don't want you too, things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T16:57:39-08:00","id":824674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=824434#post824434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize that having the Criminal Justice System actually work with any degree of efficiency would dramatically change the tone of the game, right? I mean, it's one thing to have your PCs get arrested or even imprisoned in the course of playing the game, but a lot of the overall themes of CoD rely on the system being corrupt, inefficient, and ultimately incapable of getting positive results. Nevermind that escape is just a few die rolls away for most Beasts, and that staying on the run is easier than you'd think, what you have to ask yourself, 'is what I'm about to do worth it for the cops to pursue?&quot; Most of the time, short of noticeable property damage or readily discovered victims with clearly mundane injuries and/or relatively sober and lucid accounts of what happened, there is very little the authorities can do to turn a reported crime into an arrest, much less a conviction.<br /> <br /> Long story short: if you have any degree of crossover, or play smart, the strict legality of what you are doing to Feed should not be an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus it's not as if a Beast is completely powerless against people with badges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T03:42:26-08:00","id":824891,"title":"","content":"You have to keep in mind that the beast can evade law enforcement relatively easily thanks to their powers: Opening a primordial pathway allows them to disappear form the crime scene, then they can open another pathway to a different location to get an ironclad alibi: &quot;The witnesses claiming to have seen me setting the fire must be mistaken as at the time I was clearly at the other end the city buying an engagement ring - I'm sure the store has surveillance cameras which you can check.&quot;<br /> Hiding either the stolen goods (for a collector) or the dead bodies (for predators) in the lair will also make it difficult to prosecute the crimes even if the beast does not have an alibi. Then there are nightmares which can be used to derail the investigation, You Must Obey could be used to force a policeman to destroy evidence, while pretty much any nightmare can be used to make a witness look insane. In short as long as the criminal system thinks its dealing with mundane crimes it is easy to spoof with supernatural means.<br /> <br /> However, as others have pointed out there are legal feeding opportunities. One is ironically enough to join the law enforcement, which would give nemesis and predators perfectly legal means of satisfying their hunger while chasing down suspects. Tyrants can feed by intimidating people during traffic controls, collectors can search for evidence to sate their hunger and ravagers could feed by destroying the suspects life.<br /> <br /> Other legal ways of satisfying ones hunger would be any competitive game where a tyrant feeds by beating his opponents while a collector is after the trophies. Some games like paintball could even feed a predator while he tracks down opponents. Literally any hierarchy could be the feeding ground of a Tyrant. Journalism would also work for both predators and nemesis (hunting a good story and exposing crimes respectively).<br /> <br /> Apart of such mundane ways to feed your hunger there are also countless options to feed on other supernaturals. A collector might start to venture into the hedge and gather gobblin fruits, while a predator could help the forsaken to hunt down claimed and the pure and so on.<br /> <br /> So there are more than enough legal methods to feed and if those are not sufficient you can always rely on your supernatural abilities to throw the police of your trail.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T04:58:14-08:00","id":824899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law#post824164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be a silly question... oh... alright this is a silly question. Anyway I realized that in order to suppress his hunger, a beast need to commit actions which thecnically are all crimes which I suppose soon or later, will lead the police at the beast's house door. My question is: there's no way to feed in a more reserved way and without break laws?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. The more moral of Beasts even do so. <br /> <br /> But beings sloppy with feeding isn't quite going to attract police. Its going to start attracting Heroes who migth happen to have been cops at one point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T17:16:48-08:00","id":825160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=824899#post824899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure. The more moral of Beasts even do so. <br /> <br /> But beings sloppy with feeding isn't quite going to attract police. Its going to start attracting Heroes who migth happen to have been cops at one point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus there groups of werewolves who embed themselves in the police. Plus I'm betting Ghouls and Nemisis/ Predator beasts who are police officers and detectives. So yeah, don't be sloppy when feeding and any supernatural police officers (and fellow beasts) won't opt to kick your ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T05:18:10-08:00","id":825362,"title":"","content":"There's also changelings who are heavy into police to help track down Huntsmen, because of the whole murder thing. Plenty of mages and vamps with fingers in that pie too. So, yeah. Good way to piss off other supernaturals, who are a threat as well.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying, though, that if you're sloppy enough feeding your Hunger that you're attracting mortal police, chances are that at least one of those police officers is going to end up waking up as a Hero. Feeding sloppy enough to attract mortal attention of any kind is basically the main trigger for someone becoming a Hero. So, if you attract police attention, chances are you'll be facing hero / hunter attention in there as well.<br /> <br /> I wonder if we'll get a Hero-based Conspiracy in the Mortal Remains equivalent for BtP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T16:44:09-08:00","id":825655,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys for all your hints!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T02:43:28-08:00","id":827366,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking I may be oriented for a not too much vicious kind of hunger: maybe a nemesis who is a strict teacher, but disciplinary notes, low grades or also sending a student to the principal, can count as punishment?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T03:29:17-08:00","id":827382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=827366#post827366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking I may be oriented for a not too much vicious kind of hunger: maybe a nemesis who is a strict teacher, but disciplinary notes, low grades or also sending a student to the principal, can count as punishment?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It would suffice for low Satiety I think, but you'd need something more for higher ones. You'd need to terrify the students though. It's the fear they feed off, not the act itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:57:52-08:00","id":827421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=827366#post827366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking I may be oriented for a not too much vicious kind of hunger: maybe a nemesis who is a strict teacher, but disciplinary notes, low grades or also sending a student to the principal, can count as punishment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ms. Blaise, the assistant principal Tyrant is still in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:33:43-08:00","id":827542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=827366#post827366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking I may be oriented for a not too much vicious kind of hunger: maybe a nemesis who is a strict teacher, but disciplinary notes, low grades or also sending a student to the principal, can count as punishment?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe punish the kids like that for low Satiety, and then punish bad parents more harshly for higher Satiety. Doesn't have to be obvious it's the teacher doing the punishing. Use nightmares to scare them into being better parents, or get them committed and the kids adopted by better parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:08:58-08:00","id":827554,"title":"","content":"That's the kind of Beast I like to play, one who uses his Hunger for 'noble' (insofar as anything in WoD can be noble) ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T10:07:23-08:00","id":827595,"title":"","content":"And what about a Tryant VIP Manager, which plans his celebrity's whole daily schedule and always try hard to negotiate the best terms for his client? (or is still too gentle for a Beast?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T10:11:30-08:00","id":827599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=827595#post827595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what about a Tryant VIP Manager, which plans his celebrity's whole daily schedule and always try hard to negotiate the best terms for his client? (or is still too gentle for a Beast?)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. As long as there's a demonstration of force, literal or not, that imposes the will of the Beast over others and makes clear more often than not who's running the game, it fits. Considering what some managers do both in real life and in media, there's fertile ground for a Tyrant in there.<br /> <br /> I remember reading some tales about Elvis' manager that pretty much scream &quot;Tyrant Beast with tons of XP here&quot;!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-10-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T10:15:34-08:00","id":827600,"title":"","content":"Arliss was a Beast of a show, very horrible. Definitely something you can do. There's tons of legal ways to Feast.<br /> <br /> Generally the idea with this, really all the games, is that you can always 'just get by.' A Beast can just Feast a little, vampires can just drink enough from animals to get up in the evening, werewolves can literally just hunt legally sanctioned prey. But games tend to force those people into situations where they need to make choices. They may need to use more energy to deal with something that comes up, an enemy might threaten their small supply, and so forth.<br /> <br /> I mean, it could be fun for some people to just play a game about getting by without anything popping up. But I have to imagine it's a small percentage of players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T10:31:58-08:00","id":827608,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, what happens when my teacher example needs a high Satiety meal but there isn't any really bad parents to punish? Maybe a parent who is not great, but not really terrible. Now the Beast has to choose, compromise their system a little bit and feed or go into a situation without the right amount of Satiety. This is what makes it a dramatic story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T10:37:25-08:00","id":827609,"title":"","content":"Beast's drama in a nutshell. It's simple once you get it but that does not make it less powerful. It's really one of the things I appreciate the most about this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T14:57:58-08:00","id":828448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=827599#post827599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not. As long as there's a demonstration of force, literal or not, that imposes the will of the Beast over others and makes clear more often than not who's running the game, it fits. Considering what some managers do both in real life and in media, there's fertile ground for a Tyrant in there.<br /> <br /> I remember reading some tales about Elvis' manager that pretty much scream &quot;Tyrant Beast with tons of XP here&quot;!</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that cheating and saboting rivals in order to clean the path for your VIP suits for a tryant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:06:46-08:00","id":828451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=828448#post828448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think that cheating and saboting rivals in order to clean the path for your VIP suits for a tryant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sound right to me. You're demonstrating that you have power and doing so in a way that benefits you, albeit indirectly. That's a Tyrant right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:13:44-08:00","id":828456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=828448#post828448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think that cheating and saboting rivals in order to clean the path for your VIP suits for a tryant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly. In a way, you're showing that they're weak for not having the skill and shrewdness to predict or stop your actions. It's a sea full of sharks out there and if they can't swim well, they better stay away from the water.<br /> <br /> Just be sure to do so in a way that clearly demonstrates your superiority or involvement while at the same time leaving them without a way to retaliate more often than not. It might not be obvious at first, but Tyrants live for the moments their victim realize they're on the losing side and bringing those victims to it a big part of the Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:15:29-08:00","id":828459,"title":"","content":"Something like using a nightmare to persuade an opponent to forfait? Maybe they know that the tryant is involved, but cannot prove it due to it's supernatural nature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 02-11-2016, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:04:05-08:00","id":828541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=828459#post828459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something like using a nightmare to persuade an opponent to forfait? Maybe they know that the tryant is involved, but cannot prove it due to it's supernatural nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or hell maybe they write it off as nerves or pressure about the whole thing and decide to back out because they think they can't win. Also maybe you end up making a hero, so you know be careful around former political rivals lest your death becomes ammo for their future political rivals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T05:17:29-08:00","id":828736,"title":"","content":"It's very hard to find a good balance: if I'm too soft the horror will strave and if I'm too reckless heroes will come...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 02-12-2016, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T05:33:01-08:00","id":828746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/824164-feeding-and-the-law?p=828736#post828736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very hard to find a good balance: if I'm too soft the horror will strave and if I'm too reckless heroes will come...</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes a bit of patience, yeah, but it comes easier with practice. Also remember that the hungrier you are the easier are the requirements. If you're low Satiety any demonstration of power and strenght will do.<br /> <br /> That's before considering the other methods of recovering Satiety, like the always useful Family Dinner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}